       "children": [
        {
         "t": "heading",
         "level": "p",
         "text": "Why it matters",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "heading",
         "level": "h2",
         "text": "What Makes a Good Doctor or Clinic Logo?",
         "align": "left",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "text",
         "html": "<p>A good medical logo looks professional, reassuring and simple. Patients are often anxious, in a hurry or comparing several practices on a phone screen, so the logo should be clear before it is clever. Clean typography, a restrained palette and a symbol that fits your specialty do more than a busy illustration.</p><p>It also has to work in some unglamorous places: the header of an intake form, a name badge, an appointment reminder text, a building directory and a lobby wall. We design a full version and a compact mark, test them at small sizes and in one color, and avoid overused symbols that make every clinic look the same.</p>",
         "align": "left",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "list",
         "items": [
          {
           "text": "Legible typography for older patients and small print",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          },
          {
           "text": "Colors that feel calm without looking generic",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          },
          {
           "text": "A compact icon for portals, apps and social profiles",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          }
         ],
         "classes": []
        }
       ]
      },
