       "classes": []
      },
      {
       "t": "heading",
       "level": "h2",
       "text": "Medical Logo Design FAQs",
       "align": "center",
       "classes": []
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "accordion",
     "items": [
      {
       "q": "What colors work best for a medical logo?",
       "a": "<p>Blues and greens are popular because they read as calm and trustworthy, but they are also very common. Teal, navy, warm gray or a single accent color can help you stand out while staying professional. We test every palette for readability on forms and signs.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "Can I use the caduceus or a red cross in my logo?",
       "a": "<p>We usually advise against it. The red cross emblem is legally protected and reserved for specific uses, and the caduceus is often used incorrectly for medicine. A custom symbol tied to your specialty is more distinctive and avoids those issues.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "Do you design logos for dentists, therapists and med spas too?",
       "a": "<p>Yes. We design logos for physicians, dental offices, physical therapists, counselors, chiropractors, med spas, veterinary clinics, home health agencies and medical transportation companies.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "How much does a medical practice logo cost in Austin?",
       "a": "<p>Custom logo design at Logo Design Austin is priced from $125 to $175, depending on complexity, with no upfront payment. You pay after you approve the final design.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "Will my logo work on scrubs and office signs?",
       "a": "<p>Yes. You get a full version for signs and print plus a simplified version for embroidery on scrubs and lab coats, along with one-color versions for engraving or frosted glass.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "What files do I receive?",
       "a": "<p>You receive vector files (AI, EPS, SVG and PDF) for sign companies and printers, plus transparent PNGs for your website, patient portal, email signature and social media.</p>"
      }
     ],
     "classes": []
    }
   ]
